<title>USA: U.S. to donate farm commodities to Georgia.</title>
<headline>U.S. to donate farm commodities to Georgia.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture said Friday it will donate $3.2 million of U.S. farm commodities to the Salvation Army World Service Office for distribution to needy citizens in Georgia.</p>
<p>The commodities include 1,750 tonnes of wheat flour, 1,750 tonnes of vegetable oil, 1,750 tonnes of rice and 1,250 tonnes of kidney beans.</p>
<p>The donation will be made under USDA's Food for Progress program.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8394</p>
</text>
